Patric Mueller wrote on Mon, 21 Mar 2011 21:29:30 +0100:

> Regardless of that issue wouldn't you also have to limit *bad luck* to
> balance it?

No.  The phenomonon you call "bad luck" is a well-deserved punisment.

More seriously, bad luck does not imbalance the metagame, while good luck 
does.  

> > startscummers don't generally
> > agree on what exactly it is they should startscum for).

That's because most startscummers aren't terribly good at the game. 

> I think professional players agree that the starting inventory and
> even the starting stats are not at all important in Vanilla if you
> don't do a conduct ascension.

I disagree. Sure, with good play any character is ascendable, but there 
is a huge difference between starting with 18 STR&CON vs 9 STR&CON.  Or 
starting with rings of conflict and regeneration vs rings of stealth and 
protection from shapechangers.

> > What does rgrn suggest should be prevented from happening, 
> > to avoid getting lucky early?
> 
> Dark mines?
> No early coaligned altar?
> Guaranteed cross-aligned altar in mine town?

I think that's going a bit far.  Perfect balance isn't needed, merely 
enough so that ascensions aren't delegitimized.  I don't think we'll have 
people saying "well, of course player X managed to do conduct Y -- he 
found a coaligned altar on DL3".  



